From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] journal: defer reattach while GTK4 canvas is still rooted

GTK4 can leave a detached Journal canvas rooted until the current dispatch
cycle completes.  Appending that widget immediately to the canvas area then
aborts in gtk_widget_root().  Defer only this transient case; normal canvas
changes remain synchronous and retain the existing GTK4 ownership boundary.

--- a/src/jarabe/journal/journalwindow.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/journal/journalwindow.py
@@ -18,4 +18,4 @@
 import logging
 _logger = logging.getLogger('JournalWindow')
 
-from gi.repository import Gtk, Gdk
+from gi.repository import Gtk, Gdk, GLib
@@ -77,2 +77,6 @@
             if widget.get_parent() != self._canvas_area:
+                if widget.get_root() is not None:
+                    # GTK clears the root one dispatch turn after unparent().
+                    GLib.idle_add(self.set_canvas, widget)
+                    return
                 self._canvas_area.append(widget)
